{
  "dom_id": "step-e7454",
  "name": "Example: Computing the Area Scale Factor of a Linear Transformation",
  "problem": "What is the area scale factor of the linear transformation $\\mathbf{T}$ that is given by its standard matrix \n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}2 & 3 \\\\ 1 & 4\\end{aligned}]\n$$",
  "worked_solution": "The area scale factor of a linear transformation $\\mathbf T$ with standard matrix $T$ is equal to $|\\det(T)|.$ Therefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}|det(T)| & =|2\\cdot 4-3\\cdot 1| \\\\  & =|8-3| \\\\  & =5.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
  "calculator_instructions": "",
  "fields": [],
  "result": null,
